WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.497
An anti-join pattern answers a very useful question
which left-side rows have

00:00:04.511 --> 00:00:09.576
no related record We begin with a LEFT JOIN because
we want

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:14.421
to preserve every patient When a patient has no lab
result columns

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:18.723
from lab results are NULL We then filter for a
right-side key

00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:24.527
test ID being NULL Run the query and inspect the
result

00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:28.885
In this dataset the returned patient should be
someone who has no

00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:33.697
lab result at all The choice of column in the NULL
test

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.845
matters A primary key such as test ID is a good
choice

00:00:37.858 --> 00:00:41.437
because a matched lab row cannot legitimately have a
NULL primary key

00:00:43.179 --> 00:00:46.679
Read the logic in plain English keep all patients
try to match

00:00:46.705 --> 00:00:49.863
lab rows then keep only the patients for whom no lab
row

00:00:49.876 --> 00:00:55.391
matched This same pattern can find customers with no
orders students

00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:58.035
with no submissions or products with no sales
